Z||000013||Phoenix||09-06-2000||12:31 PM||||I wanted to get one when spy photos and press releases started in the early 80's, never did though. Bought an 88 coupe last spring and wished I had bought one in 88  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  43 years old.||||reg||1
Z||000014||mbramble||09-06-2000||12:52 PM||||I was out of the country with the military for the entire production period.  I never even heard of one until my daughter bought one (just because she liked how it looked) in '94 after she graduated high school.  When she got married she sold it to her brother.  After having some problems with it and not feeling comfortable taking it to NY when he got stationed there for some Navy nuc training, my son "gave me" the car for the $300 he owed me.  It sat around for over a year with only starting it up occassionally to keep the battery up.  Finally decided I was gonna let my youngest drive it but because it ran so poorly I was afraid he get hung out in the middle of an intersection and get creamed. That's whn I ran across this forum, when I was trying to get some info on what might be wrong with it.  Took it to the Pontiac dealer and they replaced a bad coil pack and it's been running great every since.  My 17 year old is now driving it to school everyday.  3rd kid in the family to drive it!!  And though he would prefer that he had something else, he has lately been following the forum and asking about things like swapping the coupe fascia for a GT one.  He helped sand and polish the turbo wheels I bought used off ebay, etc.<P>We both like the car.  I'm 45.  Sorry for the long post!!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 09-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Standard||09-06-2000||02:00 PM||||Well, I'm 19 and I have 2  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I wanted one ever since I first found out what they were.. I enjoy uniqueness  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000016||bHooper||09-06-2000||02:03 PM||||i bought my 86.5 GT in November '89... when I was 23... and I still have that car.<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000017||Homicidal||09-06-2000||02:04 PM||||18 here!  Had it since I was 17.  I know two guys in the area that have one also, one 18 also and the other 23.<P>I bought one because I needed a replacement car QUICK.  Never knew I would love this car so D@MN much!!!<P>Far from an "old man's" car.  <P>||||reg||1
