Z||000034||Blade||09-07-2000||02:47 PM||||Well im 29 had my fiero 2 weeks its been a fun car so far. I got the car cuz it was a deal i couldnt refuse. 600 for 86 se v6. Now imjust trying to get it fixed up and trying not to get any tickets. having this car has also made me wanna get my sunbeam alpine back on the road(it was my high school car, woulda been during the years the fiero came out.) Hhehehe i remember racing a few fieros back in the day against my alpine. Actually now im keeping my eye out for other cheap fieros :P<P>Blade||||reg||1
Z||000035||BellaFiero||09-07-2000||03:29 PM||||19 years old... a 1985 GT that I rescued and a perfect ( to my tastes ) '88 coupe that's been customized to a certain fiery place and back. Always loved the Fiero since I first saw it ( I was about six when I first saw one ). Played with the hotwheels cars and I've always wanted one. First car when I was sixteen was an old-school muscle car, a Plymouth Fury. Then I sold it and bought a Ford Tempo, which I put miles on it as many teenagers do ( running around and generally doing nothing but having a great time of it ) and then we MADE it a one-way convertible ( whoops, no roof... why'd you swing that hacksaw like that?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ). Always on the lookout for my next dream car, I saw her in a Schnucks parking lot for sale. Using the money from the Fury, I picked her up and began customizing. Trans Am racing stripes from NFS High Stakes, Cobra mini jet scoop, Fi-Air-O over-the-roof twin scoops, spoiler, GT fascias, custom polished red aluminum shifter for my automatic, and a boomin' Aiwa system.... and now I'm going to restore an 85 GT. But I'll keep her stock - one semi-domestic-riced 4 cyl, one real 6er.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Four cylinders are my fave, though - coolest looking 4 banger in the world.||||reg||10
