Z||000040||jmw||09-08-2000||06:37 PM||||Chalk up another one for the over-30 group. I am 35, fixing to turn 36. My Dad worked for GM and got my red '84 SE as a company car when they first came out. I fell in love with it and my Mom talked him into keeping it for me. My Dad, who's about 6'2", always complained that he couldn't get in and out of it. He'd been telling me for years to get another car (these last few years I've had a lot of problems with it), but now he's really excited that I've gotten into "restoring" it. Anwyay, up until last February, I drove my Fiero every day from the time I was 19. The only reason I got a second car is because I had to travel for work and couldn't afford to get stranded. I love Fieros now more than ever and, even though mine is pretty beat up, I enjoy driving her much more now than I did before.  <P>Sorry so long. Fun topic. Great forum.||||reg||7
